        "original_id": "7f2a6405-bc23-5e49-9919-abfca2753ab9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Geoffrey Cheshire, Leonard Cheshire\n- Roles: father, war hero, Royal Air Force pilot, philanthropist, founder\n- Organizations: Cheshire Foundation Homes for the Sick\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Geoffrey Cheshire was the father of Leonard Cheshire.\n- Leonard Cheshire was born on 7 September 1917 and died on 31 July 1992.\n- Leonard Cheshire was an English war hero and a highly decorated World War II Royal Air Force pilot.\n- Leonard Cheshire held the titles Group Captain Geoffrey Leonard Cheshire, Baron Cheshire, and VC.\n- Leonard Cheshire was a philanthropist and founded the Cheshire Foundation Homes for the Sick.",
